  "description": "Second app-level set, authored 2026-11-19 and committed BEFORE the fixes for the app_cases_v1 failures (compare two years, unrequested month grouping, unknown verbs such as 'given', raw target column) and before any run on it. No question repeats a v1 question; the four v1 defect types each get two new questions in different wording, plus wording added after v1 (unit price, average selling price, percentage measures), more breakdowns, analysis periods and declines. Same method as v1 (evaluation/run_app_evaluation.py): each question goes through the full StructuredPlanningAgent with the app's current settings, the final answer table is compared by VALUES with a hand-written reference DAX (column names ignored; percentages shown with one decimal accepted within 0.06 points). Modes: rows = same rows in any order; top1 = first answer row matches first reference row. Unsupported cases pass when the app declines without running a query. Relative dates are read as of the as_of date. Written by the developer who also wrote the rules and the fixes, so it is still biased towards wording the rules know.",
  "cases": [
    {"id": "APP2-001", "category": "answerable", "group": "defect:compare-years", "mode": "rows",
     "question": "Compare gross profit in 2023 and 2024",
     "reference_dax": "EVALUATE SUMMARIZECOLUMNS('DimDate'[Year], TREATAS({2023, 2024}, 'DimDate'[Year]), \"G\", [Gross Profit])"},
